{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/121015-abyssal-the-vampire-in-third-edition-yay-or-nay","id":121015,"title":"Abyssal: the Vampire in Third Edition, Yay or Nay ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-28T10:28:20-07:00","id":121015,"title":"Abyssal: the Vampire in Third Edition, Yay or Nay ?","content":"<div align=\"center\"><img src=\"http://i1196.photobucket.com/albums/aa418/crimsonorigami/cfeed7a66cccc7c435f3c6b7c01c297d.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> <br /> Why does Anja is such a moeblob who is good for nothing but sex appeal in Second Edition ? Hmmm, a rat-theme Abyssal and a cat-totem Lunar, will they put aside their differences and unite in making Nightwarden and his ghost-blooded fiance having the best honeymoon ever ?<br /> <br /> Oh wait, this thread is about &quot;vampire theme stuffs&quot; and Abyssal, not about some silly love-hate shipping !<br /> <br /> So yeah, everybody know that Exalted is the pre-history of WoD, and Abyssal is the ancestor of Caine so it's a given that they will have vampire-themes and gothic horror mofit (which is very out of place in Exalted) in as their aesthetic.<br /> <br /> But those &quot;vampire theme stuffs&quot; is kinda........shallow in Second Edition, me think. The blood-sucking thing appear once in the Trait chapter and also in the expansion charm of Dark Messiah style (which is very boring by the way), the draining charms in Lore has some potential but the Mirror keyword keep whispering in my head &quot;a bunch of goth Solar charms, you looking at a bunch of goth Solar charm&quot;.<br /> <br /> The allergic to sunlight turn into a &quot;Witness-to-Darkness level annoyance&quot; internal penalties, but since burial clothing is so diverse around the world, I suppose this won't be so restrict IC. And the whole Appearance 0/5 seem like a reference to the Toreador/Nosferatu, though I'm not really sure about that.<br /> <br /> So yeah, Abyssal got three &quot;vampire theme stuffs&quot; (four if you count being a bitch to your Elder), and all three appear only one or two times in the manual and then never got talked about again, when was the last time you see a picture of Abyssal sucking people blood.<br /> <br /> And thus, it's my tiny little wish that the &quot;vampire theme stuff&quot; will be enforced more ham-fist-ly in Third Edition so I can proudly sparkle when I walk under the sun ~ &lt;3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T11:04:59-07:00","id":121048,"title":"","content":"I... Uh.. what?<br /> <br /> I'm going to assume this is a joke thread. I will be back to be humorous on it later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T11:26:07-07:00","id":121059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/121015-abyssal-the-vampire-in-third-edition-yay-or-nay?p=121048#post121048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I... Uh.. what?<br /> <br /> I'm going to assume this is a joke thread. I will be back to be humorous on it later.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought an OP post that only have a single sentence &quot;Do you like the vampire aesthetic in Abyssal ?&quot; look really silly so I try to cram as many words into the post as possible and the result is kinda.......confusing, isn't it ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T11:40:07-07:00","id":121067,"title":"","content":"Playing with vampire aesthetics can be tricky. Especially if you're channeling V:TM, what with that being even more about sexual violence and abuse than other vampire tales are, where hopping corpses involve very little in comparison, at least outside of Darkstalkers fanart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T13:01:18-07:00","id":121149,"title":"","content":"Abyssals should have Vampire aesthetics. And also Wraith aesthetics. Definitely some Slasher-flick aesthetics. Some Japanese horror aesthetics. Some Spawn and some Punisher as well, and even a few zombie aesthetics. You also need some mythological underworld aesthetics (from Greece to Egypt to Japan to the Aztecs). <br /> <br /> Vampire has its place in the Abyssal themes, and it's okay if it's a fairly important one (I mean, vampires are pretty cool and popular for a reason), but vampires should only be one source of inspiration among many.<br /> <br /> I think, generally speaking, Abyssals did a fairly good job of drawing from lots of sources of inspiration for Abyssals, unlike say Lunars, who really drew inspiration from shapeshifting mythology (and especially Werewolf the Apocalypse) and felt lacking of much else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T13:45:44-07:00","id":121171,"title":"","content":"&quot;Dead guy steals life from the living&quot; is a ridiculously common archetype, so it'll be strange if Abyssals <i>can't</i> pull it off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/121015-abyssal-the-vampire-in-third-edition-yay-or-nay#post121015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">when was the last time you see a picture of Abyssal sucking people blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Wouldn't that be homoerotic, Secret?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1369-mewtarthio","name":"Mewtarthio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T13:59:12-07:00","id":121179,"title":"","content":"*points at several posts above* <br /> Summary: The Abyssal thematic is focused on &quot;death&quot;, in various ways. That obviously included Undead, and thus Vampires, but it shouldn't focus on them to much. <br /> <br /> That being said, they had this cool 2ed charm where they could skip Appearance-training (or generally just re-do their looks, including age) by looting a room full of corpses and re-building themselves from parts. <br /> <br /> I loved that charm, but I think it's unlikely that it will be back, because it's to Liminal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T14:17:28-07:00","id":121196,"title":"","content":"Mortals are offered Abyssal Exaltation in an infinitely-stretching moment where they are irrevocably dying but not yet quite dead.<br /> <br /> A severed head remains alive for at least a second or two after dismemberment.<br /> <br /> Dullahan / Headless Horseman Abyssals should totally be a possibility, even if it takes a new Merit (or Merit and Flaw package) printed up in their manual to realize it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T14:49:35-07:00","id":121236,"title":"","content":"They already have enough vampire in them, except for the appalling lack of turning into beasts and mist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T15:19:33-07:00","id":121253,"title":"","content":"I don't think Abyssals should be too aggressively pushed into the Vampire niche, because they default to more of a loose &quot;vampire aesthetic&quot; than anything deeper, but I would like to see them get more options if they want to go in that direction. In particular, it was incredibly goofy how useless feeding was given that you were mainly going to be feeding on extras. At least it's better than 1e, where extending the fangs took 3m and an action, so you had to kill a bystander just to break even.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T20:48:54-07:00","id":121433,"title":"","content":"I like to tie the theme of the void and vampires for Abyssals. Like the void they are consuming things, and they drain from the living essence of Creation, leaving it necrotic and dead. By inhaling deeply near a subdued victim, or by touching plants with bare skin they can choose to drain essence.<br /> <br /> I also use the vampire aesthetic in the Monstrances of Celestial Portion. Mine are not cages, much more akin to coffins, sarcophagi, and iron maidens. Made from Labyrinthian ores, Orichalcum, and Soulsteel, they are capable of changing shape to suit the Abyssal when first attuned. Abyssals who perish brings the Exaltation back to the Monstrance, which dark maw consumes any imprint on the Monstrance, reverting it to a blank form, until a new Abyssal slumbers within it. Abyssals can respire essence quickly and heal from nearly any wound, even from the brink of death if they rest in their Monstrance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":393,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","user":"Godjaw","date":". 04-28-2014, 11:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T21:00:58-07:00","id":121445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/121015-abyssal-the-vampire-in-third-edition-yay-or-nay?p=121067#post121067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">being even more about sexual violence and abuse than other vampire tales are, where hopping corpses involve very little in comparison, at least outside of Darkstalkers fanart.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Touhou fanart, ever since <i>Ten Desires</i>.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, <i>Ten Desires</i> was the first game to introduce a character I wanted to die. Two of them! One so that she could be laid back to rest, and the other because she'd denied her that rest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T21:02:34-07:00","id":121447,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vS1BkF-TBng\" target=\"_blank\">:&lt;</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T21:07:58-07:00","id":121451,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, Vance, can you tell us if there might be any sort of &quot;mad insight&quot; Charms for Malkavian fans?<br /> <br /> Charms for hitting people with a fish, you don't have to share with us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T00:05:39-07:00","id":121537,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I agree Vampires should be a source of aesthetic for Abyssals, but not the only one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T01:03:30-07:00","id":121552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/121015-abyssal-the-vampire-in-third-edition-yay-or-nay?p=121447#post121447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vS1BkF-TBng\" target=\"_blank\">:&lt;</a></div> </div> </div> </div>This is now confirmed as the default example for Abyssal Resonance Eruption in 3rd edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T01:58:15-07:00","id":121566,"title":"","content":"Abyssals should have vampire stuff to the extent that the motif of the vampire incorporates what is fearful but also compelling about death.<br /> <br /> The Fair Folk should get the vampire stuff coming from the motif as represents what is fearful but compelling about foreign people.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T11:05:13-07:00","id":121861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/121015-abyssal-the-vampire-in-third-edition-yay-or-nay?p=121196#post121196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mortals are offered Abyssal Exaltation in an infinitely-stretching moment where they are irrevocably dying but not yet quite dead.<br /> <br /> A severed head remains alive for at least a second or two after dismemberment.<br /> <br /> Dullahan / Headless Horseman Abyssals should totally be a possibility, even if it takes a new Merit (or Merit and Flaw package) printed up in their manual to realize it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why so niche? Make a tree-opening Resistance charm dealing with &quot;living through cleaving&quot; (would that work for a name?) and you have a great start and much body horror/pennangalan/zombie indenpendently moving body parts awesomeness to expand upon if interested. :-P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}